<title>ITALY: Banco Napoli issues 200bln lire of bonds.</title>
<headline>Banco Napoli issues 200bln lire of bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Italian bank, Banco di Napoli, said on Friday it was issuing two bonds worth a total 200 billion lire which will be sold through its various branches.</p>
<p>Banco di Napoli said it would offer 50 billion lire of two year paper with a 5.15 percent coupon and 150 billion lire of five year paper with a six percent coupon. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
